{"by_variant":{"minimalsanitized":[{"id":"CA1","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[97],"code":"uint256 collateralPrice = oracle.getAssetPrice(msg.sender);","security_function":"ROOT_CAUSE","rationale":"ROOT_CAUSE - Fetches collateral price from manipulable Curve pool oracle. Attacker drains pool liquidity to inflate reported price, deposits at inflated value."},{"id":"CA2","type":"COMPUTATION","lines":[148],"code":"uint256 price = (balance1 * 1e18) / balance0;","security_function":"ROOT_CAUSE","rationale":"ROOT_CAUSE - Price calculation uses spot balances from Curve pool. Large swaps can manipulate balance0/balance1 ratio to inflate or deflate price."},{"id":"CA3","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[144,145],"code":"uint256 balance0 = curvePool.balances(0);\nuint256 balance1 = curvePool.balances(1);\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Balance reads within oracle. Implementation detail of CA2 - the vulnerability is the price formula, not the reads themselves."},{"id":"CA4","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[98],"code":"uint256 borrowPrice = oracle.getAssetPrice(asset);","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Borrow price fetch. Not required for exploit - inflated collateral alone is sufficient to borrow max."},{"id":"CA5","type":"EXT_CALL","lines":[83],"code":"IERC20(asset).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Token transfer in deposit."},{"id":"CA6","type":"STATE_MOD","lines":[84],"code":"deposits[onBehalfOf] += amount;","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Deposit state update."},{"id":"CA7","type":"COMPUTATION","lines":[103,104,105,107],"code":"uint256 collateralValue = (deposits[msg.sender] * collateralPrice) / 1e18;\nuint256 maxBorrow = (collateralValue * LTV) / BASIS_POINTS;\nuint256 borrowValue = (amount * borrowPrice) / 1e18;\n","security_function":"BENIGN","rationale":"Borrow value calculations. Correct arithmetic that applies manipulated price - vulnerability is in the price source, not these computations."},{"i